    "plan_id": "pilot01_sonnet55extra_qwen3_1_7b",
    "target_model": "Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B-Base",
    "hypothesis": "Caveat: Section 1 (48 layers, hidden 896) and Section 2 (28 layers, hidden 2048, k/v [1024,2048], packet ID qwen3_1_7b) describe different shapes. To stay valid under either, every op is scale_tensor, which is shape-agnostic, on layers 12-26 only, and I avoid q_proj/k_proj, biases and norm weights because they may be absent or cancelled by q_norm/k_norm. Rationale: multilingual LMs tend to process in a language-agnostic, English-leaning latent space in mid layers and realize the target language in late layers. Slightly damping mid-depth MLP writes (down_proj, -3%) may reduce English-pivot interference. Slightly amplifying mid-late o_proj (+3%) may strengthen context retrieval for MCF reading comprehension and cultural questions. Slightly amplifying late MLP down_proj (+4-5%) may sharpen Filipino/Cebuano token realization and the low generation scores (tatoeba, ntrex, tico19). Whole-tensor scaling at |delta| >= 0.03 survives bf16 rounding, whereas narrow spectral bands would mostly round away. Magnitudes are small (<=5%, 9 tensors, well under the Frobenius/L_inf caps), and layers 0-1, 7 and 23, plus the final norm and embeddings, are skipped to avoid outlier-feature or massive-activation directions and keep fluency intact. Signs are an untested prior, not a measured result.",
